<p>Man, I was all set to enjoy this as just a bizarre slice of weirdness but the last three logs just didn't click for me the way the logs of the instances did. It made all the disparate entities feel artificial, their interactions felt kind of forced.</p>
<p>I was expecting something to escalate, maybe like what <a href="/scp-1454">SCP-1454</a> did with giving identical clones a fresh personality, but instead it just retreads what's already been established for another thousand words and then calls it quits.</p>
<p>The note at the end is very generic and it frankly feels like this article lost what was making it unique and original about halfway through. I love the idea of the former Austrailian Prime Minister being an anomaly but apart from the altered versions this just doesn't make the most of an awesome concept.</p>
<p>It could have been brilliant, but for now it's just a major letdown. Downvoted but I hope this gets reworked sometime. I'd love to see a version of this that fixes its flaws.</p>

