<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Instances may be informed of the existance of other instances, but are not to be allowed contact with other instances.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Existence. And the amount of 'instance' make this read awkwardly. I'd suggest a tweak like &quot;Instances may be informed of each other's existence , but are not to be allowed contact.&quot;</p>
<p>and here:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Each specific instance of SCP-3477 has specialized containment procedures relating specifically to that instance.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Each specific instance of SCP-3477 has specialized containment procedures relating to its specific properties.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>For full containment details specific to each instance, consult Document-3477 #1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;For specialized containment details, consult Document-3477 #1.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3477 is a large collection of anomalous humanoids, each claiming to be the 17th Prime Minister of Australia Harold Holt (henceforth referred to as SCP-3477-0).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;large&quot; is superfluous; it can be cut.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>While each instance of SCP-3477 is different in anomalous properties</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;While each instance displays unique anomalous properties&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>For example, each instance of SCP-3477 claims to have contacted individuals related to their chosen method of gaining immortality on . The majority of individuals that they have claimed to met with have been found and confirmed the stories of their respective SCP-3477 instances.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Reads as incredibly redundant given the sentence this footnote it's sourced to. The next part could begin:</p>
<p>&quot;e.g. SCP-3477-8 claims to have met with Ottaviano Medici (a Marshall, Carter and Dark salesman) on that November 20th, 1967 at their personal house.&quot;</p>
<p>3477-19 seems like a good place to link <a href="/scp-2736">SCP-2736</a>, just sayin'.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Also, I've been on fire for the past sixty years.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I just died! This is great.</p>
<hr />
<p>I like the first interview, but I would maybe change the instance log to remove or replace -34, so the interview comes across a bit fresher (not further detailing an instance that was already introduced). Agreeing in that it falls off for me after that - while the meeting itself is entertaining, it seems like forcing the idiot-ball onto the SCPF, specifically to set-up the containment breach&#8230;which itself was rather trite.</p>
</div>
