			<div class="content" id="post-content-3589542">
									

<p>I really like this story. It made me hypothesise that whatever he did to become immortal opened up a wormhole to 34 alternate universes and all the other immortal Harolds fell into this one. Kind of like a wormhole&#8230; but a funnel to capture all quantum possibilities.</p>
<p>There is some fun quantum choice stuff going on here. At the point he did whatever magic he did, that congregated all the quantum choices into one reality and dumped them into our universe.</p>
<p>Dunno if I am explaining this right. Imagine playing roulette and performing some quantum funny business, so that suddenly 37 roulette tables appear and the ball lands on each number possible. Table 1 lands on 1, table 2 lands on 2&#8230; etc up to 37. Or opening up Schroedinger's box and finding 2 cats, one alive and one dead.</p>

							</div>

								
